    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (82.15), both of whom benefit from highly favorable matchups against back-end rotation arms. **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, capitalizing on a weak 4.96 xERA matchup for Ryan Johnson; his projection is further buoyed by a 16% park factor boost and a massive 19% bump for the SP skill profile, overriding the minor negative impact of the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) emerges as a surprisingly strong UTIL start, utilizing an impressive 19% SP skill advantage against Andrew Abbott to climb well above his base projection despite being a left-on-left matchup.\n\nPlatoon edges are the primary catalyst for our mid-tier starts, with **Luis Robert Jr.** (64.13) and **Jackson Merrill** (60.87) both leveraging park and SP factors to maintain \"Strong\" status. **Luis Robert Jr.** remains a focal point for our scarce stolen base category, gaining a 4% efficiency boost from the slow delivery of Foster Griffin. The toughest bench decision centered on **Miguel Vargas** (51.78); while his xwOBA of .388 is elite, he was ultimately squeezed out of the starting nine by the specific positional needs and the slightly higher stability of **Denzer Guzman** and **Dominic Smith** in their respective matchups. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, as these scores assume standardized hitting positions. **Sam Antonacci** (43.95) represents our highest risk today; he is forced to contend with a difficult left-on-left platoon against Ranger Suarez and a negative SP skill adjustment (-11%). While we rely on his leadoff spot to capture value, he sits firmly at the floor of our starting criteria. We continue to manage our remaining bench depth, including **Nasim Nunez** and **Luis Lara**, closely, though neither currently offers the necessary ceiling to displace our current starters against their specific daily matchups.",
